{"symbol":"RHEB","resolved":{"input":"RHEB","symbol":"RHEB","ncbi_gene_id":"6009","name":"Ras homolog, mTORC1 binding","location":"7q36.1","aliases":["RHEB2"],"uniprot":"Q15382","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"RHEB function (UniProt Q15382, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): Small GTPase that acts as an allosteric activator of the canonical mTORC1 complex, an evolutionarily conserved central nutrient sensor that stimulates anabolic reactions and macromolecule biosynthesis to promote cellular biomass generation and growth. In response to nutrients, growth factors or amino acids, specifically activates the protein kinase activity of MTOR, the catalytic component of the mTORC1 complex: acts by causing a conformational change that allows the alignment of residues in the active site of MTOR, thereby enhancing the phosphorylation of ribosomal protein S6 kinase (RPS6KB1 and RPS6KB2) and EIF4EBP1 (4E-BP1). RHEB is also required for localization of the TSC-TBC complex ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q15382","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q15382/entry","title":"RHEB: GTP-binding protein Rheb"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12172553","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12172553/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12271141","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12271141/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12842888","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12842888/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12869586","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12869586/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"RHEB GO biological process annotations: cellular response to nutrient levels, positive regulation of TOR signaling, positive regulation of TORC1 signaling, regulation of type B pancreatic cell development","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q15382","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q15382/entry","title":"RHEB: GTP-binding